  "limitations": [
    "Edges are aggregated with the attack label in the grouping key, so these are not deployment-valid estimates.",
    "With the trained-head consultant every loop comparison is separated under the two-level bootstrap (loop above AGAF, the GNN rung and the LLM rung, 3 seeds). With the superseded whitened-prototype consultant nothing was separated on either dataset; that earlier state is preserved under `supersedes`.",
    "Training-seed variance is measured; fold-partition variance is NOT (the split is fixed at seed 42). The reported std is a lower bound on total uncertainty.",
    "The real-versus-head_only ablation combines feedback injection and final semantic fusion, and does not attribute the gain between them. The mechanism-only experiment (output fusion off) does: neither realistic consultant is separated from control through the injection path, while the oracle is separated on both datasets. Under the superseded prototype consultant the injected bias was ~0.02-0.08 on unit-variance features (archive 2026-09-06, Finding 3); under the trained head it is ~1.33.",
    "The selected top_k_percent and injection_scale were optimized on rotating validation folds; nested cross-validation or an untouched set is required for a fully unbiased final estimate."
